    "title": "RCB vs. CSK, IPL 2026: Tim David heroics set up 43-run win for Bengaluru | Sporting News India",
    "text": "Royal Challengers Bengaluru scored a dominant 43-run win over Chennai Super Kings in IPL 2026 at the M. Chinnaswamy Stadium on Sunday.After a strong start, Tim David played the finisher role to perfection, scoring 70 off just 25 balls to lift RCB to 250/3 in their 20 overs. CSK's disappointing start to the 2026 season continued as they folded for 207 for their third straight defeat. In this article, The Sporting News tracks the IPL 2026 match and provides each team's live win probabilities.Add The Sporting News as a preferred news sourceRCB vs CSK IPL 2026: Live win probability and toss winner resultAfter 19.4 overs, CSK are 207/10CSK have been bowled out for 207. A mini-collapse of the top order, and they could not recover from the early setback. They have lost all three matches.After 15.1 overs, CSK are 165/7Prashant has gone back to the dugout after scoring 43 runs. The tail is out and CSK need 86 runs in the final five overs. Tough task at hand. After 10 overs, CSK are 109/6CSK are staring at a massive defeat in Bengaluru. They have lost more than half of the side, and Prashant Veer remains their only hope. Krunal Pandya and Jacob Duffy have taken two wickets each. After 6.1 overs, CSK are 77/4CSK are in trouble as they have lost their top four batsmen for just 77 runs. The pressure of the scoreboard is telling. The top three batters scored in single digits. Samson was dismissed for 9. Sarfaraz shone the brightest with a quickfire 50 from 25 balls. After 20 overs, RCB are 250/3It was absolute carnage from Tim David, who scored 70 from 25 balls. His innings was adorned by eight towering sixes and three boundaries. This is the highest team score in IPL 2026.After 16 overs, RCB are 172/3RCB have accelerated at a sensational pace and have scored 81 runs in the last six overs. Patidar has scored 40 from 14 balls. They should target 220 at this stage. After 10 overs, RCB are 91/1RCB have added 40 runs in the next four overs. Salt is doing the bulk of the heavy lifting with Padikkal playing the role of a foil. After six overs, RCB are 51/1It is a decent start for RCB as they reached 50 in the first six overs. However, the loss of Kohli has hurt them. Toss: CSK won the toss and elected to field first.RCB vs. CSK: Playing XIRoyal Challengers Bengaluru playing XI: Phil Salt (wk), Virat Kohli, Rajat Patidar (c), Devdutt Padikkal, Jitesh Sharma, Krunal Pandya, Tim David, Romario Shepherd, Bhuvneshwar Kumar, Jacob Duffy, Abhinandan SinghImpact options: Jacob Bethell, Suyash Sharma, Rasikh Salam, Kanishk Chouhan, Venkatesh IyerChennai Super Kings playing XI: Sanju Samson(w), Ruturaj Gaikwad(c), Ayush Mhatre, Sarfaraz Khan, Shivam Dube, Prashant Veer, Jamie Overton, Noor Ahmad, Anshul Kamboj, Matt Henry, Khaleel AhmedImpact options: Matthew Short, Akeal Hosein, Kartik SharmaRCB vs CSK IPL 2026: Win percentageTeamWin probabilityRCB100%CSK0%RCB vs CSK IPL 2026 odds Related links:Today's match in IPL 2026Live cricket matches todayAll the latest cricket newsAll the IPL-related news",
